{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "advection_1d_nonuniform_zero_grad",
    "description": "MMS driver: 1-D linear advection u_t = -c u_x + c g'(x) on the unit interval [0, 1] discretized on a SMOOTHLY STRETCHED non-uniform mesh by grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/rules/central_D1_nonuniform_zero_grad_bc (second-order centered nonuniform interior with second-order one-sided walls). Forced-steady manufactured solution u(x,t) = g(x) = cos(pi x), constant in time: substituting into u_t = -c u_x + c g'(x) gives 0 = -c g'(x) + c g'(x) exactly, so the exact field is steady and the source is S(x) = c g'(x) = -c pi sin(pi x). The discrete drift away from g is exactly the operator truncation error on the stretched mesh, which is second-order in L2 (supraconvergence) even though the pointwise truncation is O(h) where the spacing varies (LeVeque 2007 section 2.13). cos(pi x) has zero gradient at x=0 and x=1, matching the one-sided zero-gradient-family wall closure. The mesh follows the grid's EDGE-ARRAY contract (grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm): the consumer supplies ONE node array xe (shape [x_nodes], N+1 values) for the quadratic stretch x(xi) = 0.6 xi + 0.4 xi^2 on uniform computational nodes xi_k = (k-1)/N, i.e. xe[k] = 0.6 ((k-1)/N) + 0.4 ((k-1)/N)^2 (xe[1]=0, xe[N+1]=1), and the GRID derives the cell centers xc from it via nonuniform_cell_center -- a first derivative needs only centers, not the control widths dxw, so dxw is not materialized. A loader-API rebinding of N re-sizes x_nodes and re-derives the whole mesh consistently. The forcing observed src = c g'(x) reads xc at runtime (a runtime expression position where the free-name geometry resolves), while the initial condition and test references spell the stretched cell center xc[i] = (xe(i-1)+xe(i))/2 inline from literals and the metaparameter name N alone (the build-time 6.6.5/ic cellwise evaluation is scope-free; AGENTS.md build-time scope caveat), algebraically identical to the grid-derived xc, so the t=0 assertion is exact.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_nonuniform_1d",
      "equation:advection",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.13 (nonuniform grids) and the supraconvergence discussion."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Advection": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/rules/central_D1_nonuniform_zero_grad_bc.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Advected tracer field over the x index set."
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Constant transport speed."
        },
        "xe": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "x_nodes"
          ],
          "description": "Node (edge) coordinates of the quadratic-stretch mesh, xe[k] = 0.6 ((k-1)/N) + 0.4 ((k-1)/N)^2 for node k = 1..N+1 (xe[1]=0, xe[N+1]=1): the grid's single geometry input over the N+1-member node axis x_nodes. N is the document-scoped metaparameter substituted at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so a convergence-sweep rebinding of N re-derives the nodes. Aggregation index `k` over x_nodes."
        },
        "xc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Cell centers, GRID-DERIVED from xe by applying grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d nonuniform_cell_center (xc[i] = (xe[i]+xe[i+1])/2). Read by the rule body for the center-to-center stencil spacings and by the forcing observed src."
        },
        "src": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/(m^3 s)",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "MMS forcing S(x) = c g'(x) = -c pi sin(pi x) that makes u = cos(pi x) an exact steady solution of u_t = -c u_x + S. A runtime expression position, so it reads the grid-derived cell centers xc by index (the free-name geometry resolves at evaluation). Aggregation index `i` over x."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "cos",
