      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_transport_nonuniform_zero_grad",
          "description": "Forced-steady manufactured solution u(x,t) = cos(pi x) with c = 1 on the quadratic-stretch mesh (b=0.4). Source S(x) = c g'(x) = -c pi sin(pi x) makes u steady: u_t = -c u_x + S = 0. cos(pi x) has zero wall gradient (one-sided zero-gradient-family closure compatible). References evaluate at the stretched cell centers xc[i] = (xe(i-1)+xe(i))/2, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and the metaparameter N only), algebraically identical to the grid-derived xc observed used at runtime. The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring; the t=0.1 assertion bounds the L2 error, which falls at the supraconvergent order 2. Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_nonuniform_zero_grad/golden/errors.json.",
